    "reference_source_mechanism": [
      "Traditional RSA NotifyAuthenticated/NotifyDisconnected enqueue CK/DC without Interrupt in android-15.0.0_r1 libadbd_auth; AUTH3 prompt and TLS device events call Interrupt.",
      "Framework CK handler updates the full-string connection map, calls setLastConnectionTime and schedules persistence; setLastConnectionTime can reinsert a removed key.",
      "ALLOW and CK/DC are tracked by full public-key strings including comments, while RSA mathematical verification and displayed fingerprints use the key material.",
      "The actual removed and reinserted RSA A strings both used runner@. Comment inconsistency is an additional bookkeeping defect, not a sufficient explanation for this reinsert.",
      "Unpair does not clear the connected-key map in the reference implementation; periodic updates can refresh keys from that map.",
      "Waiting for a DC for every signed RSA reconnect is not justified by the reviewed reference call path or these actual logs."
    ],
    "causal_confidence": "High confidence that the observed interruption followed an actual delayed RSA A CK and persistence, independent of TLS A authentication. Pinned AOSP provides a directly matching queue/handler mechanism, but is not exact binary provenance for the Google Play build.",
    "comment_only_fix_sufficient": false,
    "chosen_next_isolation": "Separate rsa/tls CI jobs with fresh disposable AVDs; same adbd PID/listener within each TLS acceptance matrix; no widened authorization set.",
